//------------------------------------------------------------------------
// vliw -- execution datapath (largest block, ~35k lines)
//
// Consumes the decoded micro-op stream (instrc) from deco and executes
// it, driving I/O reads/writes (readio_data/writeio_data/io_add).
// Instantiates the readable behavioral sub-blocks:
//   arithbox      (arithbox.v)     -- ALU operations
//   shiftbox      (shiftbox.v)     -- shift/rotate operations
//   synthetic_op  (synthetic_op.v) -- microcoded/synthesized op sequences
// plus a very large number of private auto-generated AWDP_*/AWMUX_*
// helper cells (adders, comparators, muxes) for its internal datapath.
// Instantiated as `i_vliw` in cpu (see v586_cpu.v).
//
// NOTE: gate-level netlist below the port list (aside from the three
// instantiated readable sub-blocks above) -- see the header of
// v586_biu32_axi.v for what that means and README.md for the hierarchy map.
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

